From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phononenom <64574232+Phononenom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:44:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the Vulkan port on the new core

tools/prepare-vulkan-port.py derives the PS5's Vulkan files from the core's; its anchors and replacements
follow nx2 (PrepareDraw's signature, the collector's new argument, the staging IsFree walks, the pipeline
cache's serializer), and it carries the port's memory work: image and buffer refusals handled instead of
ending the session, the give-back that also takes costly and GPU-written images in an emergency, the
memory-short branch's ages, uniform buffers through FindBindingBuffer. headless/CMakeLists.txt's anchors
(multiplayer, the guest clock, frame generation) and the small Vulkan .inc files likewise. The host checks
that read these files follow them.

From these commits (oldest first):
- 2026-11-17 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the Vulkan anchors on Lichii 907d54757b
- 2026-11-17 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the configure-time edits on Lichii 907d54757b, but the JIT's
- 2026-11-17 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the PS5 layer on Lichii's NUP reader, its pending parts left out
- 2026-11-17 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the PS5 layer builds and links on Lichii 907d54757b
- 2026-11-17 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the build's checks on Lichii 907d54757b
- 2026-11-17 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: headers the core keeps are not shadowed by an earlier build's copies
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the ASTC transcode bound never submits under the texture's staging copy
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the memory trace counts images' host bytes
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: an allocation out of device memory gives memory back and asks again
- 2026-11-18 fixup! Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the memory trace counts images' host bytes
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the collectors answer refused allocations, not a full pool
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the memory trace shows decode images and multi-range buffers
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the driver's zero block is allocated while the pool is empty
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: recovery packs at most 256 MiB for one try, none for huge allocations
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: a built-in patch's state in BSS is accepted past the patch buffer
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the Vulkan display takes the output resolution's mode
- 2026-11-19 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the staging pressure check knows the reserve
- 2026-11-19 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the memory trace breaks ASTC textures down by block size
- 2026-11-19 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: who holds the graphics allocator's memory
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the layered texture upload survives a refusal
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the collector keeps a rescaled image it cannot copy back
- 2026-11-22 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the give-back's pass may delete costly images while a write waits
- 2026-11-22 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: four host checks follow the Lichii nx2 c363fafe26 core
